      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RIDE HIGH CAPTIN (4) look close to a win after placing in his last four outings. Led and stuck on well when beaten 1.6m as runner-up at Kilmore last time. Draws well again and deserves to break through. COGNAC COWBOY (1) made an encouraging return when edged out by just a head as runner-up at Kilmore. Fitter for that and is lightly raced with upside. The ace draw could see him go one better. There was merit in the debut effort of BAD GRANDMA (6) when fourth after drawing on the back row and racing wide in the latter stages. Open to improvement. HILLCROFT HUSTLER (7) did a good job to come from this barrier for second on debut at Cranbourne. Could progress off that.",
